A||N||6||cscougar||Velocity Tube||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||09-26-2001||09:24 AM||||I recently ordered and installed a velocity tube from West Coast Fieros.   This is a stainless steel tube that replaces the water separator box in the intake.  I have it now and a holley scoop.  <P>There is a very noticable increase in power and acceleration using this.  I didn't realize how restricting the water separator box was.  I would recommend this since you can still use the air filter (I use a K & N filter).  <P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||09-26-2001||10:00 AM||||Does this tube leave the air filter open to rain through the decklid grill?  Where did you get the holley scoop?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mr.Frosty||09-26-2001||10:05 AM||||It doesn't work with an open filter setup.It goes under the original filter canister,and replaces the restrictive plastic box underneath.You leave the metal filter pot where it is. <P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||09-26-2001||11:51 AM||||Do you have to cut anything to install it? How much was the tube? How about some pics?<P>Inquiring Fiero owners want to know,<BR>Rick 88||||reg||5
Z||000004||cscougar||09-26-2001||12:00 PM||||The cost is $49.99.  You dont have to remove the air cleaner....I just took loose the fender liner and reached in behind the intake on the driver side and unbolted the air box and removed it.  The tube slips into the rubber hoses that attached to the air box.  It replaces that.  After installing you can't see it but the performance is alot better.  <P>West Coast site:  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rick 88||09-26-2001||01:25 PM||||CS,<P>Thanks for the info and pics. I like the idea of retaining the factory air cleaner and still using cooler outside air. Looks to be much better than just removing the water separator. Hey did you notice our number of posts!<P>Where is China Spring TX?||||reg||7
Z||000006||cscougar||09-26-2001||02:10 PM||||China Spring is 12 miles NW of Waco, TX.  Close to Crawford, TX the home of Pres. Bush.<P>My wife is from El Paso.  Graduated in 1974 from Eastwood HS.||||reg||1
